Article 39

1. Facilitation of the establishment of service provider institutions as referred to in Article 36 paragraph (2) letter a is implemented by establishing a family learning center.
2. The stages of establishing a family learning center include:
a. preparing regulations;
b. preparing human resources;
c. preparing facilities and infrastructure; and
d. establishment of a family learning center.
3. The family learning center functions:
a. as a service institution in prevention and counseling;
b. as a referral liaison point as a solution for child and family problems;
c. strengthening family capacity in caring for and protecting children;
d. as a family learning place through education for parents; and
e. as a holistic integrative family one-stop service based on children's rights.

